# 必考词 Unit23
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit23核心词汇

{{confront}}{{/kənˈfrʌnt}}{{v. 面对； confront；对抗}}{{We must confront the problem directly.}}
{{confuse}}{{/kənˈfjuːz}}{{v. 使困惑； confuse；混淆}}{{The instructions confused many students.}}
{{congress}}{{/ˈkɒŋɡres}}{{n. 国会； congress；代表大会}}{{Congress passed the new tax bill.}}
{{conscience}}{{/ˈkɒnʃəns}}{{n. 良心； conscience}}{{His conscience would not allow him to lie.}}
{{conscious}}{{/ˈkɒnʃəs}}{{adj. 意识到的； conscious；自觉的}}{{She was conscious of the need to act quickly.}}
{{consensus}}{{/kənˈsensəs}}{{n. 共识； consensus}}{{The committee reached a consensus on the issue.}}
{{consent}}{{/kənˈsent}}{{n./v. 同意； consent；允许}}{{The patient gave consent for the operation.}}
{{consequence}}{{/ˈkɒnsɪkwəns}}{{n. 后果； consequence；重要性}}{{You must face the consequences of your actions.}}
{{conservative}}{{/kənˈsɜːvətɪv}}{{adj./n. 保守的； conservative；保守派}}{{He holds conservative views on economic policy.}}
{{considerable}}{{/kənˈsɪdərəbl}}{{adj. 相当大的； considerable}}{{The project requires considerable investment.}}
{{consist}}{{/kənˈsɪst}}{{v. 由…组成； consist；在于}}{{The team consists of twelve members.}}
{{consistent}}{{/kənˈsɪstənt}}{{adj. 一致的； consistent；始终如一的}}{{Her work has been consistent throughout the year.}}
{{constant}}{{/ˈkɒnstənt}}{{adj./n. 不变的； constant；常数}}{{The temperature remains constant throughout the day.}}
{{constitute}}{{/ˈkɒnstɪtjuːt}}{{v. 构成； constitute；组成}}{{Women constitute a large proportion of the workforce.}}
{{construct}}{{/kənˈstrʌkt}}{{v. 建造； construct；构建}}{{The bridge was constructed in the 19th century.}}
{{consult}}{{/kənˈsʌlt}}{{v. 咨询； consult；查阅}}{{You should consult a doctor about your symptoms.}}
{{consume}}{{/kənˈsjuːm}}{{v. 消耗； consume；消费}}{{The building consumes a lot of energy.}}
{{contact}}{{/ˈkɒntækt}}{{n./v. 接触； contact；联系}}{{Please contact me if you have any questions.}}
{{contain}}{{/kənˈteɪn}}{{v. 包含； contain；控制}}{{The report contains important information.}}
{{contemplate}}{{/ˈkɒntəmpleɪt}}{{v. 沉思； contemplate；考虑}}{{He contemplated the meaning of life.}}
{{contemporary}}{{/kənˈtemprəri}}{{adj./n. 当代的； contemporary；同时代的人}}{{The museum displays contemporary art.}}
{{contempt}}{{/kənˈtempt}}{{n. 轻视； contempt；蔑视}}{{He showed contempt for the rules.}}
{{contend}}{{/kənˈtend}}{{v. 竞争； contend；主张}}{{Several companies are contending for the contract.}}
{{context}}{{/ˈkɒntekst}}{{n. 上下文； context；背景}}{{The meaning of the word depends on the context.}}
{{contract}}{{/ˈkɒntrækt}}{{n./v. 合同； contract；收缩}}{{They signed a contract with the supplier.}}
{{contradict}}{{/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt}}{{v. 反驳； contradict；矛盾}}{{The evidence contradicts his statement.}}
{{contrast}}{{/ˈkɒntrɑːst}}{{n./v. 对比； contrast；差别}}{{There is a sharp contrast between the two approaches.}}
{{contribute}}{{/kənˈtrɪbjuːt}}{{v. 贡献； contribute；投稿}}{{She contributed generously to the charity.}}
{{controversial}}{{/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl}}{{adj. 有争议的； controversial}}{{The decision was highly controversial.}}
{{controversy}}{{/ˈkɒntrəvɜːsi}}{{n. 争论； controversy；争议}}{{The policy sparked a heated controversy.}}
{{convention}}{{/kənˈvenʃn}}{{n. 惯例； convention；大会}}{{By convention, the eldest son inherits the title.}}
{{convert}}{{/kənˈvɜːt}}{{v. 转换； convert；使改变信仰}}{{The building was converted into a museum.}}
{{convey}}{{/kənˈveɪ}}{{v. 传达； convey；运输}}{{The painting conveys a sense of peace.}}
{{convince}}{{/kənˈvɪns}}{{v. 使确信； convince；说服}}{{She convinced him to change his mind.}}
{{cooperate}}{{/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt}}{{v. 合作； cooperate}}{{The two companies agreed to cooperate on the project.}}
{{coordinate}}{{/kəʊˈɔːdɪneɪt}}{{v./n. 协调； coordinate；坐标}}{{The team needs to coordinate their efforts.}}
{{cope}}{{/kəʊp}}{{v. 应对； cope；处理}}{{She has learned to cope with stress.}}
{{core}}{{/kɔːr}}{{n./adj. 核心； core；核心的}}{{Innovation is at the core of the company's strategy.}}
{{corporate}}{{/ˈkɔːpərət}}{{adj. 公司的； corporate；共同的}}{{The corporate culture emphasizes teamwork.}}
{{correspond}}{{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd}}{{v. 对应； correspond；通信}}{{The data corresponds with the previous findings.}}
{{corrupt}}{{/kəˈrʌpt}}{{adj./v. 腐败的； corrupt；使腐化}}{{The corrupt officials were arrested.}}
{{counsel}}{{/ˈkaʊnsl}}{{n./v. 忠告； counsel；建议}}{{She sought legal counsel before signing the contract.}}
{{count}}{{/kaʊnt}}{{v./n. 计数； count；重要}}{{Every vote counts in a democracy.}}
{{counterpart}}{{/ˈkaʊntəpɑːt}}{{n. 对应的人或物； counterpart}}{{The CEO met with her Japanese counterpart.}}
{{couple}}{{/ˈkʌpl}}{{n./v. 一对； couple；连接}}{{A couple of students arrived late.}}
{{course}}{{/kɔːs}}{{n. 课程； course；过程；方针}}{{The course covers a wide range of topics.}}
{{crack}}{{/kræk}}{{v./n. 裂缝； crack；破解}}{{The vase has a crack in it.}}
{{craft}}{{/krɑːft}}{{n./v. 工艺； craft；精心制作}}{{She crafted a beautiful piece of jewelry.}}
{{crash}}{{/kræʃ}}{{v./n. 碰撞； crash；崩溃}}{{The stock market crashed in 2008.}}
{{creative}}{{/kriˈeɪtɪv}}{{adj. 创造性的； creative}}{{She has a very creative mind.}}
{{credit}}{{/ˈkredɪt}}{{n./v. 信用； credit；归功于}}{{The success was credited to the entire team.}}
{{criminal}}{{/ˈkrɪmɪnl}}{{adj./n. 犯罪的； criminal；罪犯}}{{Criminal activity has decreased in the area.}}
{{crisis}}{{/ˈkraɪsɪs}}{{n. 危机； crisis}}{{The country is facing an economic crisis.}}
{{criteria}}{{/kraɪˈtɪəriə}}{{n. 标准； criteria（复数）}}{{The selection criteria are clearly defined.}}
{{critical}}{{/ˈkrɪtɪkl}}{{adj. 关键的； critical；批评的}}{{Critical thinking is an important skill.}}
{{crucial}}{{/ˈkruːʃl}}{{adj. 至关重要的； crucial}}{{Timing is crucial in business negotiations.}}
{{cultivate}}{{/ˈkʌltɪveɪt}}{{v. 培养； cultivate；耕种}}{{Schools should cultivate creativity in students.}}
{{curiosity}}{{/ˌkjʊəriˈɒsəti}}{{n. 好奇心； curiosity}}{{Children have a natural curiosity about the world.}}
{{current}}{{/ˈkʌrənt}}{{adj./n. 当前的； current；水流}}{{The current situation requires immediate action.}}
{{curriculum}}{{/kəˈrɪkjələm}}{{n. 课程； curriculum}}{{The school has updated its curriculum.}}
{{custom}}{{/ˈkʌstəm}}{{n. 习惯； custom； customs（海关）}}{{It is the custom to shake hands when meeting someone.}}
{{cycle}}{{/ˈsaɪkl}}{{n./v. 循环； cycle；骑自行车}}{{The business cycle affects the economy.}}
{{database}}{{/ˈdeɪtəbeɪs}}{{n. 数据库； database}}{{The information is stored in a database.}}
{{deadline}}{{/ˈdedlaɪn}}{{n. 截止日期； deadline}}{{The deadline for submissions is next Friday.}}
{{debate}}{{/dɪˈbeɪt}}{{n./v. 辩论； debate；讨论}}{{The issue has sparked a heated debate.}}
{{decade}}{{/ˈdekeɪd}}{{n. 十年； decade}}{{The city has changed a lot over the past decade.}}
{{decay}}{{/dɪˈkeɪ}}{{v./n. 腐烂； decay；衰退}}{{The old house has fallen into decay.}}
{{deceive}}{{/dɪˈsiːv}}{{v. 欺骗； deceive}}{{He deceived everyone with his lies.}}
{{decent}}{{/ˈdiːsnt}}{{adj. 体面的； decent；相当好的}}{{She earns a decent salary.}}
{{declare}}{{/dɪˈkleər}}{{v. 宣布； declare；申报}}{{The country declared independence.}}
{{decline}}{{/dɪˈklaɪn}}{{v./n. 下降； decline；拒绝}}{{Sales have declined by 10% this year.}}
{{dedicate}}{{/ˈdedɪkeɪt}}{{v. 致力于； dedicate；奉献}}{{She dedicated her life to helping the poor.}}
{{deem}}{{/diːm}}{{v. 认为； deem；视为}}{{The proposal was deemed unacceptable.}}
{{defeat}}{{/dɪˈfiːt}}{{v./n. 击败； defeat；失败}}{{The team defeated their rivals in the final.}}
{{defend}}{{/dɪˈfend}}{{v. 防御； defend；辩护}}{{The lawyer defended his client in court.}}
{{deficit}}{{/ˈdefɪsɪt}}{{n. 赤字； deficit；不足}}{{The country has a large budget deficit.}}
{{define}}{{/dɪˈfaɪn}}{{v. 定义； define；限定}}{{How do you define success?}}
{{definite}}{{/ˈdefɪnət}}{{adj. 明确的； definite；确定的}}{{We need a definite answer by tomorrow.}}
{{delay}}{{/dɪˈleɪ}}{{v./n. 延迟； delay；耽搁}}{{The flight was delayed by two hours.}}
{{delegate}}{{/ˈdelɪɡeɪt}}{{v./n. 委派； delegate；代表}}{{The manager delegated the task to his assistant.}}
{{deliberate}}{{/dɪˈlɪbərət}}{{adj./v. 故意的； deliberate；仔细考虑}}{{It was a deliberate attempt to mislead the public.}}
{{delicate}}{{/ˈdelɪkət}}{{adj. 精致的； delicate；脆弱的}}{{The situation requires delicate handling.}}
{{deliver}}{{/dɪˈlɪvər}}{{v. 交付； deliver；发表（演讲）}}{{The company delivers goods within 24 hours.}}
{{demand}}{{/dɪˈmɑːnd}}{{n./v. 需求； demand；要求}}{{There is a growing demand for organic food.}}
{{democracy}}{{/dɪˈmɒkrəsi}}{{n. 民主； democracy}}{{Democracy requires active citizen participation.}}
{{demonstrate}}{{/ˈdemənstreɪt}}{{v. 证明； demonstrate；演示}}{{The experiment demonstrates the effectiveness of the treatment.}}
{{dense}}{{/dens}}{{adj. 密集的； dense；浓密的}}{{The city has a very dense population.}}
{{deny}}{{/dɪˈnaɪ}}{{v. 否认； deny；拒绝}}{{He denied all the charges against him.}}
{{depart}}{{/dɪˈpɑːt}}{{v. 离开； depart；出发}}{{The train departs at 8 a.m.}}
{{department}}{{/dɪˈpɑːtmənt}}{{n. 部门； department；系}}{{She works in the marketing department.}}
{{depend}}{{/dɪˈpend}}{{v. 依赖； depend；取决于}}{{The outcome depends on several factors.}}
{{depict}}{{/dɪˈpɪkt}}{{v. 描绘； depict；描述}}{{The painting depicts a rural landscape.}}
{{deposit}}{{/dɪˈpɒzɪt}}{{n./v. 存款； deposit；押金}}{{You need to pay a deposit when booking the room.}}
{{deprive}}{{/dɪˈpraɪv}}{{v. 剥夺； deprive}}{{The war deprived many children of education.}}
{{derive}}{{/dɪˈraɪv}}{{v. 源自； derive；获得}}{{The word derives from Latin.}}
{{describe}}{{/dɪˈskraɪb}}{{v. 描述； describe}}{{Please describe what happened.}}
{{deserve}}{{/dɪˈzɜːv}}{{v. 值得； deserve；应得}}{{She deserves a promotion for her hard work.}}
